WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.500
Our team’s capstone explores how to coordinate a patient-specific therapy journey across disconnected systems.

2
00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:15.500
CGT means Cell and Gene Therapy. In this project, patient identity, collected material, and the manufactured product must remain correctly linked throughout the journey.

3
00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:23.500
The client’s problem is conflicting information across patient operations, manufacturing, laboratories, Quality, and logistics.

4
00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:29.500
Coordinators need to understand what is blocked, why, and who can decide next.

5
00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:44.500
We followed a twenty-one stage FDE operating model, connecting discovery, domain and data modelling, architecture, requirements, engineering, evaluation, and operational planning.

6
00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:52.500
The application brings source evidence, different user views, and disruption previews together. Three connected demonstrations show the central controls.

7
00:00:53.500 --> 00:01:02.500
First, conflicting identity records become an owned case. Supporting evidence and an authorized decision are required before the proposed link is accepted.

8
00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:11.500
Second, a slot reservation loses its response. The system records an unknown outcome and checks what happened before retrying.

9
00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:18.500
Third, a Quality packet exposes missing evidence and blockers. Manufacturing completion alone cannot authorize release.

10
00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:24.500
The demonstrated release requires the correct evidence and Quality permission.

11
00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:34.500
The repository also contains automated tests, evaluation results, audit checks, integration contracts, security controls, continuous integration, monitoring exercises, and recovery plans.

12
00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:44.500
The core workflow operates with AI off. The optional assistant is simulated, not a live model.

13
00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:53.000
This is a synthetic academic demonstration. Real deployment still requires live integrations, enterprise access, approved policies, independent assurance, and measured business outcomes.

14
00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:59.500
Our principle is simple: evidence before status, and human authority before automation.

